45 780 Td
(   theta_1 + phi = 90 deg => theta_1 = 90 deg - phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore: sin\(theta_1\) = sin\(90 deg - phi\) = cos\(phi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting into the entrance equation:) Tj
T*
(   n0 * sin\(theta_0\) = n1 * cos\(phi\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Imposing the Condition for Waveguiding \(TIR\):) Tj
T*
(   - For total internal reflection at the cladding boundary, we require phi >= theta_c, where) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta_c\) = n2 / n1.) Tj
T*
(   - When phi = theta_c, the entrance launch angle reaches its maximum permissible value, termed) Tj
T*
(   the Acceptance Angle theta_a:) Tj
T*
(   n0 * sin\(theta_a\) = n1 * cos\(theta_c\) = n1 * sqrt\( 1 - sin^2\(theta_c\) \).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute sin\(theta_c\) = n2 / n1:) Tj
T*
(   n0 * sin\(theta_a\) = n1 * sqrt\( 1 - \(n2 / n1\)^2 \) = sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Acceptance Angle and Numerical Aperture Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Acceptance Angle in air \(n0 = 1.0\):) Tj
T*
(   theta_a = arcsin\( sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \) \).) Tj
T*
(   - Numerical Aperture \(NA\) is defined as the sine of the acceptance angle in air:) Tj
T*
(   NA = sin\(theta_a\) = sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \) / n0.) Tj
T*
(   - For air \(n0 = 1\):) Tj
T*
(   NA = sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \) = sqrt\( \(n1 - n2\) * \(n1 + n2\) \).) Tj
T*
(   - Using fractional index difference Delta = \(n1 - n2\) / n1 and approximating n1 + n2 ~= 2*n1:) Tj
T*
(   NA = sqrt\( \(n1 * Delta\) * \(2 * n1\) \) = n1 * sqrt\( 2 * Delta \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
