/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Classify optical fibers based on: \(a\) refractive index profile \(step-index vs graded-index\), and \(b\) mode propagation \(single-mode vs multi-mode\). Compare their physical dimensions and transmission characteristics.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Classification by Refractive Index Profile:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Step-Index \(SI\) Fiber:) Tj
T*
(   * The core has a uniform refractive index n1 throughout its cross-section.) Tj
T*
(   * At the core-cladding boundary \(r = a\), the index drops abruptly in a single step to n2.) Tj
T*
(   * Ray propagation: Light travels in straight zig-zag lines through total internal reflections.) Tj
T*
(   * Intermodal dispersion is severe due to differing geometric path lengths.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Graded-Index \(GI\) Fiber:) Tj
T*
(   * The core refractive index varies continuously as a function of radial distance r:) Tj
T*
(   n\(r\) = n1 * sqrt\( 1 - 2*Delta*\(r/a\)^alpha \) for r <= a, and n\(r\) = n2 for r > a.) Tj
T*
(   \(Optimal profile exponent alpha ~= 2.0, parabolic index profile\).) Tj
T*
(   * Ray propagation: Light rays follow smooth sinusoidal or helical curved paths due to) Tj
T*
(   continuous refraction.) Tj
T*
(   * Rays traveling longer geometric paths spend more time in lower-index outer glass where light) Tj
T*
(   speed is higher \(v = c/n\), dramatically equalizing transit times and reducing modal dispersion) Tj
T*
(   by up to 1000 times.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Classification by Mode Propagation:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Single-Mode Fiber \(SMF\):) Tj
T*
(   * Extremely small core diameter \(typically 8 to 10 micrometers\).) Tj
T*
(   * Normalized frequency V <= 2.405, allowing only the fundamental HE11 \(LP01\) mode to propagate.) Tj
T*
(   * Zero intermodal dispersion; bandwidth limited only by chromatic dispersion.) Tj
T*
(   * Dominates long-haul telecommunications and high-precision civil interferometric sensing.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Multi-Mode Fiber \(MMF\):) Tj
T*
(   * Large core diameter \(50 to 62.5 micrometers for telecom; 100 to 1000 microns for industrial) Tj
T*
(   sensing\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
