/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   microns with overtones at 1383 nm, 950 nm, and 725 nm. Advanced dehydration processes \('dry) Tj
T*
(   fibers'\) eliminate the 1383 nm water peak.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rayleigh Scattering Loss:) Tj
T*
(   - Caused by sub-microscopic random thermal density and dopant concentration fluctuations frozen) Tj
T*
(   into the silica network during glass solidification from melt \(~ 2000 C\).) Tj
T*
(   - Attenuation follows Rayleigh's law: alpha_R proportional to 1 / lambda^4.) Tj
T*
(   - At 850 nm: alpha_R ~= 1.5 dB/km; at 1310 nm: alpha_R ~= 0.35 dB/km; at 1550 nm: alpha_R ~=) Tj
T*
(   0.15 dB/km.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Radiative Bending Losses:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Macrobending Loss: Occurs when a fiber is bent around a curved structural radius) Tj
T*
(   comparable to centimeters. Evanescent field in cladding must travel faster than c/n2 to keep) Tj
T*
(   phase with core wavefront, radiating power outward into the buffer coating.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Microbending Loss: Microscopic localized axial perturbations \(micron scale\) along the) Tj
T*
(   core caused by lateral pressure, uneven cable jacketing, or temperature contraction during) Tj
T*
(   concrete setting, coupling guided modes into unguided radiating cladding modes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Achieving 0.2 dB/km at 1550 nm:) Tj
T*
(   - At 1550 nm, Rayleigh scattering has declined to ~ 0.15 dB/km while infrared silica absorption) Tj
T*
(   has just begun to rise \(~ 0.03 dB/km\).) Tj
T*
(   - In pure silica core fibers with fluorine-doped cladding \(eliminating germanium scattering) Tj
T*
(   centers\), total attenuation reaches an astounding theoretical minimum of 0.15 to 0.18 dB/km.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
