(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the expression for intermodal \(modal\) dispersion in a step-index multi-mode optical fiber. Explain how graded-index profiling drastically mitigates pulse broadening.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Origin of Intermodal Dispersion:) Tj
T*
(   - In a multi-mode step-index fiber, light rays travel along different geometric paths) Tj
T*
(   corresponding to different spatial modes.) Tj
T*
(   - Faster modes travel along the central axis, while higher-order modes follow steep zig-zag) Tj
T*
(   reflections.) Tj
T*
(   - Differences in propagation time cause an initial short light pulse to spread in time \(pulse) Tj
T*
(   broadening Delta_t\) as it travels down fiber length L.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Derivation for Step-Index Fiber:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Minimum Travel Time \(Axial Ray, phi = 90 deg\):) Tj
T*
(   The axial ray travels straight down the core axis of length L at speed v = c / n1:) Tj
T*
(   t_min = L / v = \(L * n1\) / c.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Maximum Travel Time \(Extreme Ray at Critical Angle, phi = theta_c\):) Tj
T*
(   The steepest guided ray reflects at the critical angle theta_c where sin\(theta_c\) = n2 / n1.) Tj
T*
(   The actual zig-zag path length traversed is L_path = L / sin\(theta_c\) = L * \(n1 / n2\).) Tj
T*
(   The time taken is: t_max = L_path / v = [ L * \(n1 / n2\) ] / \(c / n1\) = \(L * n1^2\) / \(c * n2\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) Total Pulse Broadening \(Intermodal Delay Delta_t\):) Tj
T*
(   Delta_t_modal = t_max - t_min = \(L * n1^2\) / \(c * n2\) - \(L * n1\) / c = \(L * n1 / c\) * [ \(n1 /) Tj
T*
(   n2\) - 1 ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(L * n1 / c\) * [ \(n1 - n2\) / n2 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Since n1 ~= n2, \(n1 - n2\) / n2 ~= Delta \(fractional index difference\):) Tj
T*
(   Delta_t_modal ~= \(L * n1 * Delta\) / c.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Mitigation in Graded-Index \(GI\) Fibers:) Tj
T*
(   - In a parabolic graded-index fiber, refractive index n\(r\) decreases with radius r.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
