(   [Problem Statement]: Explain chromatic \(intramodal\) dispersion in single-mode fibers. Distinguish between material dispersion and waveguide dispersion, and explain dispersion shifting.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Chromatic Dispersion Concept:) Tj
T*
(   - In single-mode fibers, intermodal dispersion is zero because only one mode propagates.) Tj
T*
(   - However, no optical source is perfectly monochromatic \(spectral linewidth Delta_lambda != 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Chromatic dispersion occurs because different spectral components of the light pulse travel) Tj
T*
(   at slightly different group velocities v_g.) Tj
T*
(   - Total chromatic dispersion parameter: D_total = D_mat + D_wg \(expressed in ps / \(nm * km\)\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Material Dispersion D_mat:) Tj
T*
(   - Arises from the intrinsic wavelength dependence of the silica refractive index n\(lambda\) due) Tj
T*
(   to molecular electronic resonances.) Tj
T*
(   - Material dispersion coefficient:) Tj
T*
(   D_mat = - \(lambda / c\) * \( d^2 n / d lambda^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - For pure fused silica, d^2n / dlambda^2 crosses through zero at lambda = 1270 nm \(Zero) Tj
T*
(   Material Dispersion Wavelength\), being negative below 1270 nm and positive above.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Waveguide Dispersion D_wg:) Tj
T*
(   - Arises from the physical waveguide geometry of the core and cladding.) Tj
T*
(   - The effective group velocity depends on the distribution of optical power between the core) Tj
T*
(   \(index n1\) and cladding \(index n2\).) Tj
T*
(   - At longer wavelengths, the mode field expands deeper into the lower-index cladding, reducing) Tj
T*
(   effective index n_eff.) Tj
T*
(   - D_wg is generally negative across communication bands.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Dispersion Shifting \(DSF\):) Tj
T*
(   - In standard single-mode fiber \(G.652\), D_mat + D_wg = 0 occurs naturally near 1310 nm.) Tj
T*
(   - However, minimum attenuation \(0.2 dB/km\) is at 1550 nm, where G.652 fiber has D ~= +17) Tj
T*
(   ps/\(nm*km\).) Tj
T*
(   - By tailoring the core refractive index profile \(triangular core with dual-cladding or) Tj
T*
(   segmented core\), waveguide dispersion D_wg can be made significantly more negative, shifting) Tj
T*
(   the zero dispersion wavelength to match the minimum attenuation window at 1550 nm) Tj
T*
(   \(Dispersion-Shifted Fiber, G.653\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
