12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working principles of Distributed Fiber Optic Sensing based on: \(a\) Optical Time Domain Reflectometry \(OTDR\), and \(b\) Brillouin Optical Time Domain Analysis \(BOTDA\) for civil infrastructure monitoring.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Limitations of Point Sensors vs Distributed Sensing:) Tj
T*
(   - Point sensors \(strain gauges, discrete FBGs\) only measure localized conditions where) Tj
T*
(   installed; uninstrumented failure zones can go undetected along long infrastructure.) Tj
T*
(   - Distributed Optical Fiber Sensing treats the entire optical fiber \(tens of kilometers\) as a) Tj
T*
(   continuous sensing medium, providing thousands of measurement points along dams, tunnels, and) Tj
T*
(   pipelines.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Optical Time Domain Reflectometry \(OTDR\):) Tj
T*
(   - An optical transmitter launches a high-power nanosecond laser pulse into one end of the) Tj
T*
(   fiber.) Tj
T*
(   - As the pulse travels, Rayleigh scattering continuously backscatters a fraction of photons) Tj
T*
(   back to an avalanche photodiode.) Tj
T*
(   - The location of an event \(break, bend, splice loss\) is determined by Time-of-Flight:) Tj
T*
(   z = c * t / \(2 * n_g\).) Tj
T*
(   - The logarithmic slope of the backscatter power trace gives local attenuation alpha\(z\) in) Tj
T*
(   dB/km.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Brillouin Optical Time Domain Analysis \(BOTDA\):) Tj
T*
(   - Based on Stimulated Brillouin Scattering \(SBS\), a non-linear interaction between a pump) Tj
T*
(   optical pulse and a counter-propagating continuous-wave \(CW\) probe beam via acoustic sound) Tj
T*
(   waves in the silica core.) Tj
T*
