(   [Problem Statement]: Calculate the cut-off wavelength lambda_c and core diameter for a single-mode step-index fiber with n1 = 1.468 and Delta = 0.003 to ensure single-mode propagation at all wavelengths above 1200 nm.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Single-Mode Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - Single-mode propagation requires V <= 2.40483 at the specified cutoff wavelength lambda_c.) Tj
T*
(   - V = \(2 * pi * a / lambda_c\) * NA <= 2.40483.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Numerical Aperture Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   - n1 = 1.468; Delta = 0.003.) Tj
T*
(   - NA ~= n1 * sqrt\( 2 * Delta \) = 1.468 * sqrt\( 2 * 0.003 \) = 1.468 * sqrt\( 0.006 \) = 1.468 *) Tj
T*
(   0.07746 = 0.1137.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculation of Maximum Core Radius a:) Tj
T*
(   - Given cutoff wavelength lambda_c = 1200 nm = 1.20 x 10^-6 m:) Tj
T*
(   a = \(2.40483 * lambda_c\) / \(2 * pi * NA\).) Tj
T*
(   - a = \(2.40483 * 1.20 x 10^-6\) / \(2 * pi * 0.1137\) = \(2.8858 x 10^-6\) / \(0.7144\) = 4.04 x 10^-6) Tj
T*
(   m = 4.04 micrometers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Maximum Core Diameter 2*a:) Tj
T*
(   - Core diameter: 2 * a = 2 * 4.04 = 8.08 micrometers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Verification at Telecommunication Wavelength 1550 nm:) Tj
T*
(   - V at 1550 nm: V = \(2 * pi * 4.04 x 10^-6 / 1.55 x 10^-6\) * 0.1137 = 16.37 * 0.1137 = 1.86 <) Tj
T*
(   2.405.) Tj
T*
(   - Securely within the single-mode operating envelope.) Tj
