(   1. Governing Strain-Wavelength Relation:) Tj
T*
(   - For pure mechanical strain at constant temperature \(Delta_T = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   Delta_lambda_B / lambda_B = \(1 - p_e\) * epsilon,) Tj
T*
(   where p_e is the effective photoelastic coefficient and epsilon is mechanical strain.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Calculation of Mechanical Strain epsilon:) Tj
T*
(   - Given: lambda_B = 1550.0 nm; Delta_lambda_B = +0.380 nm; p_e = 0.22.) Tj
T*
(   - \(1 - p_e\) = 1 - 0.22 = 0.78.) Tj
T*
(   - epsilon = Delta_lambda_B / [ lambda_B * \(1 - p_e\) ]) Tj
T*
(   - epsilon = 0.380 / [ 1550.0 * 0.78 ] = 0.380 / 1209.0 = 3.143 x 10^-4 = 314.3 microstrain) Tj
T*
(   \(muepsilon\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Calculation of Tensile Stress sigma_steel:) Tj
T*
(   - By Hooke's Law: sigma = E * epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   - E = 205 GPa = 205 x 10^9 N/m^2.) Tj
T*
(   - sigma = \(205 x 10^9 N/m^2\) * \(3.143 x 10^-4\) = 6.443 x 10^7 N/m^2 = 64.43 MPa.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Structural Assessment:) Tj
T*
(   - The measured tensile stress of 64.4 MPa is well below the yield strength of structural steel) Tj
T*
(   \(f_y = 250 - 355 MPa\), confirming that the bridge girder remains comfortably within its linear) Tj
T*
(   elastic design capacity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
