(   [Problem Statement]: A 60 km single-mode fiber link has an attenuation of 0.20 dB/km and chromatic dispersion D = 17 ps/\(nm*km\) at 1550 nm. It is driven by an optical transmitter with spectral linewidth 0.15 nm. Calculate: \(a\) total optical attenuation, \(b\) total chromatic dispersion pulse broadening, \(c\) maximum bit rate using the NRZ criterion Delta_t <= 0.7 * T_bit.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Link length L = 60 km.) Tj
T*
(   - Attenuation alpha = 0.20 dB/km.) Tj
T*
(   - Dispersion parameter D = 17 ps/\(nm * km\).) Tj
T*
(   - Source spectral linewidth Delta_lambda = 0.15 nm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Total Optical Attenuation:) Tj
T*
(   - Loss_total = alpha * L = \(0.20 dB/km\) * 60 km = 12.0 dB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Total Chromatic Dispersion Pulse Broadening Delta_t_chrom:) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_t_chrom = D * L * Delta_lambda) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_t_chrom = [ 17 ps/\(nm * km\) ] * \(60 km\) * \(0.15 nm\) = 17 * 60 * 0.15 = 153 picoseconds) Tj
T*
(   = 1.53 x 10^-10 seconds.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Maximum Bit Rate \(NRZ Criterion Delta_t <= 0.7 * T_bit\):) Tj
T*
(   - Bit period: T_bit >= Delta_t_chrom / 0.7 = 153 ps / 0.7 = 218.6 ps.) Tj
T*
(   - Bit rate: B_max = 1 / T_bit = 1 / \(218.6 x 10^-12 s\) = 4.57 x 10^9 bps = 4.57 Gbps.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
