/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical principles and architecture of Phase-Sensitive Optical Time Domain Reflectometry \(phi-OTDR\) used in Distributed Acoustic Sensing \(DAS\) for geotechnical pipeline and railway monitoring.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Working Principle of Distributed Acoustic Sensing \(DAS\):) Tj
T*
(   - DAS utilizes phase-sensitive OTDR \(phi-OTDR\) to transform a standard, unmodified fiber optic) Tj
T*
(   cable into a dense array of distributed dynamic strain and acoustic sensors.) Tj
T*
(   - Unlike conventional OTDR which uses low-coherence pulses to monitor average backscattered) Tj
T*
(   power, phi-OTDR launches highly coherent laser pulses \(coherence length > fiber length\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Coherent Interference Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Within each resolution cell of the fiber \(typically 1 to 10 m\), thousands of microscopic) Tj
T*
(   Rayleigh scattering centers scatter light with fixed phase relationships.) Tj
T*
(   - The backscattered light arriving at the photodetector forms a complex speckle interference) Tj
T*
(   pattern in the time domain.) Tj
T*
(   - When an external acoustic wave, train wheel vibration, or soil movement strikes the fiber,) Tj
T*
(   localized dynamic strain elastically alters the optical path length Delta\(n*L\) by fractions of) Tj
T*
(   a nanometer.) Tj
T*
(   - This shifts the relative optical phases of the scatterers, drastically altering the local) Tj
T*
(   Rayleigh interference trace.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Demodulation and Civil Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - Digital phase demodulation extracts the dynamic strain waveform epsilon\(t\) at acoustic) Tj
T*
(   frequencies \(from 0.01 Hz up to 50 kHz\) simultaneously at every meter along a 50 km fiber.) Tj
T*
(   - Railway Monitoring: Tracks train position, speed, axle weight, flat wheel defects, and broken) Tj
T*
(   rail detection.) Tj
T*
(   - Pipeline Security: Detects unauthorized third-party excavation, heavy vehicle encroachment,) Tj
T*
ET

