(   [Problem Statement]: A mass concrete gravity dam foundation has a 200 m long embedded FBG sensor string to monitor crack development. During impoundment, an FBG indicates a localized strain jump of +1850 microstrain. If the gauge length of this sensor section is L_g = 50 mm, estimate the physical crack opening displacement \(COD\) and assess structural risk.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Gauge length of the sensor: L_g = 50 mm = 0.050 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Measured strain jump: epsilon = +1850 microstrain = 1.850 x 10^-3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Calculation of Crack Opening Displacement \(COD\):) Tj
T*
(   - Average strain measured across a cracked concrete gauge length is: epsilon = Delta_L / L_g.) Tj
T*
(   - When a macro-crack forms, the elastic strain of uncracked concrete is negligible compared to) Tj
T*
(   the physical crack opening:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_L ~= COD.) Tj
T*
(   - COD = epsilon * L_g = \(1.850 x 10^-3\) * \(50 mm\) = 0.0925 mm = 92.5 micrometers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Structural and Hydraulic Risk Assessment:) Tj
T*
(   - Concrete cracking threshold strain in tension is typically 100 to 150 microstrain. The) Tj
T*
(   recorded 1850 microstrain confirms complete tensile rupture and crack formation.) Tj
T*
(   - According to international dam safety criteria \(e.g., ICOLD guidelines\):) Tj
T*
(   * Crack openings < 0.1 mm \(100 um\) are classified as minor micro-cracks that are generally) Tj
T*
(   self-healing through calcite autogenous precipitation under low hydraulic gradients.) Tj
T*
(   * However, if the crack is on the upstream water face, high hydrostatic uplift pressures could) Tj
T*
(   drive water into the joint, accelerating crack propagation.) Tj
T*
(   - Recommendation: Initiate continuous dynamic monitoring; if COD exceeds 0.2 mm, schedule) Tj
T*
(   pressure epoxy grouting.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
