(   [Problem Statement]: A fiber optic gyroscope \(FOG\) deployed in a tunnel boring machine guidance system uses a circular fiber coil of diameter D = 15 cm with 2000 turns of single-mode fiber. At wavelength lambda = 1310 nm, calculate the Sagnac phase shift Delta_phi_s when the TBM turns at an angular rate of Omega = 5 degrees per hour.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Coil diameter D = 0.15 m; Radius R = 0.075 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Number of turns N = 2000.) Tj
T*
(   - Enclosed area of single turn: A_1 = pi * R^2 = pi * \(0.075\)^2 = 0.01767 m^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Total enclosed area: A_total = N * A_1 = 2000 * 0.01767 = 35.34 m^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Wavelength lambda = 1310 nm = 1.31 x 10^-6 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Angular rotation rate Omega = 5.0 deg/hour = \(5.0 * pi / 180\) / 3600 rad/s = 8.7266 x 10^-2 /) Tj
T*
(   3600 = 2.424 x 10^-5 rad/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Speed of light: c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Sagnac Phase Shift Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - The fundamental Sagnac formula for counter-propagating beams in a rotating loop is:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_phi_s = \(8 * pi * A_total * Omega\) / \(lambda * c\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_phi_s = [ 8 * pi * \(35.34 m^2\) * \(2.424 x 10^-5 rad/s\) ] / [ \(1.31 x 10^-6 m\) * \(3.0 x) Tj
T*
(   10^8 m/s\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Numerator = 8 * pi * 35.34 * 2.424 x 10^-5 = 2.153 x 10^-2.) Tj
T*
(   - Denominator = 1.31 x 10^-6 * 3.0 x 10^8 = 3.93 x 10^2 = 393.) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_phi_s = 2.153 x 10^-2 / 393 = 5.48 x 10^-5 radians = 54.8 microradians.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Engineering Assessment:) Tj
T*
(   - Modern closed-loop FOGs with digital phase modulation readily detect phase shifts < 1) Tj
T*
(   microradian, providing drift-free gyroscopic orientation for TBM heading control over miles of) Tj
T*
(   subterranean excavation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
