(   molecular vibrational modes \(optical phonons\) of the Si-O-Si glass lattice.) Tj
T*
(   - Raman scattering produces two inelastically shifted sidebands:) Tj
T*
(   * Stokes Line \(lambda_S > lambda_0\): Photon surrenders energy to create an optical phonon;) Tj
T*
(   frequency down-shifted to nu_0 - Delta_nu_vib \(Delta_nu_vib ~= 13.2 THz, ~ 440 cm^-1\).) Tj
T*
(   * Anti-Stokes Line \(lambda_AS < lambda_0\): Photon absorbs energy from an existing thermal) Tj
T*
(   optical phonon; frequency up-shifted to nu_0 + Delta_nu_vib.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Temperature Dependence Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - The probability of an optical phonon existing in the glass lattice at thermal equilibrium is) Tj
T*
(   governed by Bose-Einstein statistics:) Tj
T*
(   n_phonon = 1 / [ exp\( h * Delta_nu_vib / \(k_B * T\) \) - 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Stokes Intensity: Involves phonon creation \(stimulated + spontaneous emission) Tj
T*
(   proportional to n_phonon + 1\):) Tj
T*
(   I_Stokes proportional to exp\( h*Delta_nu_vib / \(k_B*T\) \) / [ exp\( h*Delta_nu_vib / \(k_B*T\) \) -) Tj
T*
(   1 ] ~= constant \(very weak T dependence\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Anti-Stokes Intensity: Involves phonon absorption \(proportional to n_phonon alone\):) Tj
T*
(   I_Anti-Stokes proportional to 1 / [ exp\( h * Delta_nu_vib / \(k_B * T\) \) - 1 ] \(highly sensitive) Tj
T*
(   to T!\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) Ratio of Intensities:) Tj
T*
(   R\(T\) = I_Anti-Stokes / I_Stokes = \(lambda_S / lambda_AS\)^4 * exp\( - h * Delta_nu_vib / \(k_B *) Tj
T*
(   T\) \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Civil Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - By taking the ratio R\(T\), laser power fluctuations and fiber bending losses cancel out,) Tj
T*
(   providing absolute temperature measurements along road tunnels \(fire detection\), dams \(leakage) Tj
T*
(   tracing\), and power cables.) Tj
