(   [Problem Statement]: Calculate the acceptance angle and numerical aperture of an optical fiber when submerged in water \(n_water = 1.333\), if the fiber has core index n1 = 1.480 and cladding index n2 = 1.455. Contrast with its values in air.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Core refractive index n1 = 1.480.) Tj
T*
(   - Cladding refractive index n2 = 1.455.) Tj
T*
(   - Internal numerical parameter: sqrt\(n1^2 - n2^2\) = sqrt\( \(1.480\)^2 - \(1.455\)^2 \) = sqrt\() Tj
T*
(   2.190400 - 2.117025 \) = sqrt\( 0.073375 \) = 0.27088.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. In Air \(n0 = 1.0\):) Tj
T*
(   - NA_air = sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \) = 0.2709.) Tj
T*
(   - Acceptance angle: sin\(theta_a,air\) = NA_air = 0.2709 => theta_a,air = arcsin\(0.2709\) = 15.72) Tj
T*
(   degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - Total acceptance cone angle: 2 * theta_a,air = 31.44 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Submerged in Water \(n_water = 1.333\):) Tj
T*
(   - By Snell's law at fiber entrance face: n_water * sin\(theta_a,water\) = sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - sin\(theta_a,water\) = sqrt\( n1^2 - n2^2 \) / n_water = 0.27088 / 1.333 = 0.20321.) Tj
T*
(   - Acceptance angle in water: theta_a,water = arcsin\(0.20321\) = 11.72 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - NA in water: NA_water = n_water * sin\(theta_a,water\) = 0.2709 \(constant invariant property of) Tj
T*
(   the glass\), but the acceptance cone narrows to 2 * 11.72 = 23.44 degrees.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil Sensing Note:) Tj
T*
(   - When open-ended fiber sensors are immersed in flooded boreholes or underwater conduits, the) Tj
T*
(   acceptance cone shrinks by ~ 25%, reducing light coupling efficiency from external LEDs.) Tj
T*
