(   [Problem Statement]: A multi-channel FBG interrogator records data from 12 sensors embedded in a concrete deck slab. Formulate the matrix equation for simultaneous determination of 2D strain components \(epsilon_x, epsilon_y, gamma_xy\) from a delta strain rosette.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fiber Optic Strain Rosette Configuration:) Tj
T*
(   - An optical strain rosette consists of three FBG sensors oriented at known angular increments) Tj
T*
(   on a planar structural surface.) Tj
T*
(   - In an Equiangular \(Delta\) Rosette, the three gauges are arranged at angles:) Tj
T*
(   theta_1 = 0 deg, theta_2 = 60 deg, theta_3 = 120 deg relative to the x-axis.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Strain Transformation Equations:) Tj
T*
(   - The normal strain epsilon\(theta\) in any direction theta is related to Cartesian strain tensor) Tj
T*
(   components \(epsilon_x, epsilon_y, gamma_xy\) by:) Tj
T*
(   epsilon\(theta\) = epsilon_x * cos^2\(theta\) + epsilon_y * sin^2\(theta\) + gamma_xy *) Tj
T*
(   sin\(theta\)*cos\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting the three rosette angles:) Tj
T*
(   * Gauge 1 \(theta_1 = 0 deg\): epsilon_1 = epsilon_x.) Tj
T*
(   * Gauge 2 \(theta_2 = 60 deg\): epsilon_2 = epsilon_x * \(1/4\) + epsilon_y * \(3/4\) + gamma_xy *) Tj
T*
(   \(sqrt\(3\)/4\).) Tj
T*
(   * Gauge 3 \(theta_3 = 120 deg\): epsilon_3 = epsilon_x * \(1/4\) + epsilon_y * \(3/4\) - gamma_xy *) Tj
T*
(   \(sqrt\(3\)/4\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Matrix Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   - Expressing in matrix form: [ epsilon_measured ] = [ T ] * [ epsilon_cartesian ]:) Tj
T*
(   [ epsilon_1 ] [ 1.00 0.00 0.000 ] [ epsilon_x ]) Tj
T*
(   [ epsilon_2 ] = [ 0.25 0.75 +0.433 ] * [ epsilon_y ]) Tj
T*
(   [ epsilon_3 ] [ 0.25 0.75 -0.433 ] [ gamma_xy ]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Inverse Solution:) Tj
T*
(   - Inverting the transformation matrix yields exact 2D strains:) Tj
T*
(   * epsilon_x = epsilon_1) Tj
T*
(   * epsilon_y = \(1/3\) * [ 2*\(epsilon_2 + epsilon_3\) - epsilon_1 ]) Tj
T*
(   * gamma_xy = \(1 / sqrt\(3\)\) * \(epsilon_2 - epsilon_3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Principal strains and maximum shear strain:) Tj
T*
(   epsilon_p1,p2 = \(epsilon_x + epsilon_y\)/2 +- sqrt\( \(\(epsilon_x - epsilon_y\)/2\)^2 + \(gamma_xy /) Tj
T*
(   2\)^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   - Enables full-field 2D stress tensor analysis across concrete bridge decks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
