(   [Problem Statement]: An optical fiber communication link for a smart dam telemetry network has a length of 50 km and uses fiber with alpha = 0.22 dB/km. The system contains 5 fusion splices \(loss 0.08 dB each\) and 2 connector pairs \(0.30 dB each\). The laser transmitter launches -3 dBm, and the receiver sensitivity is -28 dBm. Perform a complete power budget calculation and determine if the design meets a 6.0 dB safety margin.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Transmitter and Receiver Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Launched optical power: P_tx = -3.0 dBm \(0.50 mW\).) Tj
T*
(   - Receiver sensitivity: P_rx = -28.0 dBm \(1.58 microwatts\).) Tj
T*
(   - Total allowable link loss: Loss_allowable = P_tx - P_rx = -3.0 - \(-28.0\) = 25.0 dB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Calculation of Channel Losses:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Fiber Attenuation Loss:) Tj
T*
(   Loss_fiber = alpha * L = \(0.22 dB/km\) * 50 km = 11.00 dB.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Splice Losses \(5 fusion splices\):) Tj
T*
(   Loss_splices = 5 * 0.08 dB = 0.40 dB.) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) Connector Losses \(2 connector pairs\):) Tj
T*
(   Loss_connectors = 2 * 0.30 dB = 0.60 dB.) Tj
T*
(   - Total Channel Loss:) Tj
T*
(   Loss_total = 11.00 + 0.40 + 0.60 = 12.00 dB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Calculation of Optical Power Safety Margin:) Tj
T*
(   - Power Margin = Loss_allowable - Loss_total = 25.00 dB - 12.00 dB = 13.00 dB.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Engineering Assessment:) Tj
T*
(   - The available power safety margin is 13.0 dB, which substantially exceeds the required 6.0 dB) Tj
T*
(   industry standard margin.) Tj
T*
(   - The link will operate with extraordinary reliability over decades, easily absorbing fiber) Tj
T*
(   aging and future repair splices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
