(   [Problem Statement]: Summarize the comprehensive role of fiber optics in modern civil engineering infrastructure, highlighting structural health monitoring, smart cities, and geophysical hazard mitigation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Paradigm Shift from Point Inspection to Neural Sensing:) Tj
T*
(   - Fiber optic technology transforms passive concrete and steel structures into intelligent,) Tj
T*
(   self-monitoring systems analogous to biological nervous systems.) Tj
T*
(   - By embedding thousands of optical sensors during construction, civil engineers acquire) Tj
T*
(   continuous real-time data regarding internal stresses, hydration temperatures, dynamic) Tj
T*
(   vibrations, and micro-cracking.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Structural Health Monitoring \(SHM\) Highlights:) Tj
T*
(   - Bridges & Overpasses: FBG strain rosettes and stay-cable sensors monitor live-load) Tj
T*
(   distribution, dynamic fatigue cycles, and thermal expansion joint health, preventing sudden) Tj
T*
(   catastrophic collapses.) Tj
T*
(   - Concrete & Embankment Dams: Distributed Brillouin and Raman sensors detect microscopic shear) Tj
T*
(   movements, foundation settlement, and subterranean water seepage years before surface) Tj
T*
(   emergence.) Tj
T*
(   - Tunnels & Underground Metros: Fiber convergence sensors measure ovalization under tectonic) Tj
T*
(   overburden pressure, guiding maintenance interventions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Smart Cities and Geohazard Mitigation:) Tj
T*
(   - Distributed Acoustic Sensing \(DAS\) converts standard telecom cables beneath urban streets) Tj
T*
(   into continuous seismic geophone networks for earthquake early warning, sinkhole detection, and) Tj
T*
(   traffic flow monitoring.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
